CHECK:BOOL_COMPARISON: Using comparison to false is error prone
#133: FILE: drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-core.c:797:
+	if (td->this_tune_ok == false)

Comparisons of A to true and false are better written
as A and !A.

See: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/1365563834.27174.12.camel@joe-AO722/

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'td->tune_around == 11'
#141: FILE: drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-core.c:805:
+	if ((!td->this_tune_ok && td->last_tune_ok) ||
+					(td->tune_around == 11)) {

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

